  "worked_solution": "Since the line $x=-1$ is a vertical line, a perpendicular line would need to be horizontal. So, the perpendicular line must take the form $y=k$ for some value of $k.$\n\nThe perpendicular line needs to go through the point $(-2,-3),$ which has a $y$-coordinate of $-3.$ So, the perpendicular line is $y=-3.$",
